    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG estate agents are delighted to present No 25 Glenmaroon Road, a lovely 3 bedroom (plus attic) semi-detached with an amazing c.77 foot long South facing garden. Measuring a substantial 144 sq.m/1,550 to include the large attic conversion, this fantastic home is situated on a quiet tree lined road and yet only a short walk from every conceivable amenity. \n\n25 Glenmaroon Road benefits from a spacious front driveway and wide vehicular side access which leads to a large block-built garage. The garden here is a real gem and boasts an enviable South facing orientation. This garden is c.77 foot long and is laid in lawn with a patio area towards the property and with gated pedestrian access.\n\nGenerously proportioned accommodation comprises of a welcoming entrance hallway with guest wc, sitting room to the front, a spacious dining/lounge and a kitchen to the rear. Upstairs is a tiled bathroom and three large bedrooms. Additionally, there is a spacious attic conversion on this home.\n\n25 Glenmaroon Road is ideally located on one of Palmerstown's most highly regarded and sought after roads. This property enjoys the best of both worlds, as it is away from the hustle and bustle, while still enjoying easy access to every conceivable amenity. Within close proximity of the M4/M50/M7 road networks, as well as a host of other amenities that include shops, schools, public transport, The Phoenix Park and sporting facilities.\n\nOverall, this is a fantastic family home in a most desirable location. Viewings come highly recommended, phone DNG Estate Agents on 01-6280400."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nHallway - 2.57m x 4.6m\nWide entrance hallway with carpeted flooring\n\nWC - 1.75m x .9m\nGuest wc with tiled flooring, wc, whb and access to under stair storage space\n\nSitting Room - 3.52m x 3.2m\nLight filled sitting room to the front with carpeted flooring, gas fire, ceiling coving and centre rose\n\nDining/Lounge - 3.32m x 6.67m\nSpacious light filled dining/lounge with an open fireplace, wood flooring, tv point and sliding doors to the garden\n\nKitchen - 2.49m x 4.5m min\nBright kitchen to the rear with fitted wall and floor units and access to the rear garden\n\nLanding - 2.1m x 2.66m\nWith carpeted flooring and a hot linen press\n\nBedroom 1 - 3.64m x 3.33m\nSpacious master bedroom to the front with an ensuite shower room, built in wardrobes and carpeted flooring\n\nEnsuite - 2.29m x .85m\nTiled ensuite with a shower, wc and whb\n\nBedroom 2 - 4m x 3.35m\nLarge double bedroom to the rear with carpeted flooring and built in wardrobes\n\nBedrooom 3 - 2.47m x 3.17m\nSingle bedroom to the front with carpeted flooring\n\nBathroom - 2.08m x 1.67m\nFully tiled bathroom with an electric shower, wc and whb\n\nAttic - 4.5m x 3.13m\nSpacious attic conversion with a dormer window, carpeted flooring, eaves storage space and a wc\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> c.77 foot Sunny south facing garden</li><li> Wide vehicular side access</li><li> Large block built garage</li><li> Spacious front driveway</li><li> Extended to the rear</li><li> Bright attic conversion</li><li> Chain free sale</li><li> 144 sq.m/1,550 sq.ft (Incl attic conversion)</li><li> 124.6 sq.m/1,341 sq.ft (Excl attic conversion)</li><li> Most sought after location</li><li> Double glazed windows</li><li> Oil fired central heating</li><li> Short walk to schools, shops and transport links</li><li> Easy access to city centre & Dublin airport</li><li> Convenient to Liffey Valley Shopping Centre</ul>"
      },
